      "id": "q1",
      "type": "explain",
      "q": "What did the Bohner and Schlüter (2014) replication find compared with the original towel study?",
      "a": "Both message types raised towel reuse over no message, but the descriptive norm message did not beat the standard environmental message.",
      "anchor": "#social-proof",
      "origin": "ai",
      "reviewed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "compare",
      "q": "Compare the positions of Gal and Rucker (2018) and Mrkva et al. (2020) on loss aversion.",
      "a": "Gal and Rucker argued loss aversion is much less general than claimed; Mrkva et al. replied that it is real but moderated by factors such as stake size.",
      "anchor": "#loss-aversion",
      "origin": "ai",
      "reviewed": false
    },
